6363161 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363161 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363161 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186363161 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd77d9db-96bd-55f7-b4d3-fb162ec30ec6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363161 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=20 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}{x}_{2} &=-4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting this into th