17592186410805 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410805 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6d57014e-b23a-5701-a76a-a3703de7149c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410806 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8a8d53f7-b5fc-5ce6-9a9c-54a7385b4356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410807 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8574fe5-c6b2-5e0e-b6b5-71b14a1ca898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nx=\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e50c9b4-d5fe-527c-b554-c5ae45ba5355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410808 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is ${R}^{-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158080" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nx=\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c899a77-435a-5aa3-92d4-0dc3a7b627aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410809 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410812 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410812 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6b34aecb-fc33-591a-beae-813382c608f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410812 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410813 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410813 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "70103913-067c-52aa-850c-673f2ce5ac0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410813 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410814 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410814 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8ef06eb7-a320-54c5-a67e-7c28d93f3d07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410814 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410815 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d783bc27-1d4d-5fd3-a3db-1a036831d9dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410815 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410816 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410816 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de997394-83f9-5ca3-92c7-b205bedc19d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410816 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509688 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186510486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509688